    <statement><tabular valign="middle">
<row>
<cell>The distance <m>d</m> of a point <m>P</m> to the line through points <m>A</m> and
   <m>B</m> is the length of the component of <m>\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;AP\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt;</m> that is orthogonal to
   <m>\lt B&gt;\lt I&gt;AB\lt /B&gt;\lt /I&gt;</m>, as indicated in the diagram.</cell>
<cell><IMG ALIGN="BOTTOM" BORDER="1" HEIGHT="160" SRC="/webwork2_files/tmp/anonymous/images/c60992db-53bf-3f1f-bd8b-9649d2a16296___d03ec05c-9004-3160-85d9-0887bbb98a3d.gif" WIDTH="196"/></cell>
</row>
</tabular>
<p>So the distance from <m>P = \left(-5,-3\right)</m> to the line through the
points <m>A = \left(2,-4\right)</m> and <m>B = \left(0,-5\right)</m> is <fillin characters="25" name="AnSwEr0001"/>.</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>4.02492</m>
      </p>
